 },
 "summary": "Four independent voltage comparators sharing one supply pin, with a PNP input stage whose common-mode range reaches ground and an open-collector output. They run from 3 V to 30 V and draw about 60 µA for all four, a figure that does not move with supply voltage. The output stage switches between a Darlington mode that sinks 30 mA at 2 V and a saturating mode that sinks 0.7 mA at 0.4 V. LP239, LP339 and LP2901 are characterized over different operating temperature ranges; LP2901DR is the -40 °C to 85 °C grade in a 14-pin SOIC on a 2500-piece reel. The LP239 is obsolete.",
